 {
  "id": "R-PHARMA-RPHARMA-2022-RINPHARMA_287",
  "title": "R pilot submissions to FDA",
  "authors": [
   "Ning Leng",
   "Hye Soo Cho"
  ],
  "year": 2022,
  "conference": "r-pharma",
  "conference_name": "R/Pharma",
  "section_code": "TK",
  "section_name": "Talk",
  "paper_code": "RPharma-2022-rinpharma_287",
  "pdf_url": "https://youtu.be/_nToEBDkEX8",
  "source_url": "https://rinpharma.github.io/data-pipelines/output/processed_talks.csv",
  "abstract": "On Nov 22nd, 2021, the R Consortium R Submissions Working Group successfully submitted an R-based test submission package through the FDA eCTD gateway. The submission package has been received by the FDA staff who were able to reproduce the numerical results.  This submission was an example submission package following eCTD specifications which include a proprietary R package, R scripts for analysis, R-based analysis data reviewer guide, and other required eCTD components.  To our knowledge, this is the first publicly available R-based, or open-source-language-based FDA submission to the eCTD gateway for CDER. We hope this submission package and our learnings can serve as a good reference for future R-based regulatory submissions.",
  "keywords": [],
  "lang": "en",
  "region": "Global",
  "added_at": "2026-08-06T08:04:34+00:00"
 },
 {
  "id": "R-PHARMA-RPHARMA-2022-RINPHARMA_288",
  "title": "Bundling JS for Your Shiny App",
  "authors": [
   "Maya Gans"
  ],
  "year": 2022,
  "conference": "r-pharma",
  "conference_name": "R/Pharma",
  "section_code": "TK",
  "section_name": "Talk",
  "paper_code": "RPharma-2022-rinpharma_288",
  "pdf_url": "https://youtu.be/ThmrFxQy0Dk",
  "source_url": "https://rinpharma.github.io/data-pipelines/output/processed_talks.csv",
  "abstract": "So you've started writing custom JavaScript for your Shiny app... but where do you put all this code?! Organizing JS files to be sourced within one another can be really hard to navigate from within a Shiny application.  In this talk I’ll cover what bundling for JS means, and how to do it in the context of Shiny. This talk should empower you to not only write code in JavaScript but bring modern tooling to your app that will allow for organization and cleaner code.",
  "keywords": [],
  "lang": "en",
  "region": "Global",
  "added_at": "2026-08-06T08:04:34+00:00"
 },
 {
  "id": "R-PHARMA-RPHARMA-2022-RINPHARMA_289",
  "title": "Building Shiny Frameworks: Some Lessons",
  "authors": [
   "Harvey Lieberman"
  ],
  "year": 2022,
  "conference": "r-pharma",
  "conference_name": "R/Pharma",
  "section_code": "TK",
  "section_name": "Talk",
  "paper_code": "RPharma-2022-rinpharma_289",
  "pdf_url": "https://youtu.be/bkKe_kC83iQ",
  "source_url": "https://rinpharma.github.io/data-pipelines/output/processed_talks.csv",
  "abstract": "It is relatively simple to create a powerful visualization app using shiny, but what if you need to change your data wrangling process or wish to build a different output?  How easy is it to provide this flexibility without having to rewrite the underlying code?  This presentation will highlight shiny frameworks - apps that are adaptable and extensible.  We shall illustrate how separation of data, application and presentation promotes flexible content and how interpreters can build app components at runtime.",
  "keywords": [],
  "lang": "en",
  "region": "Global",
  "added_at": "2026-08-06T08:04:34+00:00"
 },
 {
  "id": "R-PHARMA-RPHARMA-2022-RINPHARMA_290",
  "title": "Working at the intersection of Biostatistics and Software Engineering in a Pharma company",
  "authors": [
   "Daniel Sabanes Bové"
  ],
  "year": 2022,
  "conference": "r-pharma",
  "conference_name": "R/Pharma",
  "section_code": "TK",
  "section_name": "Talk",
  "paper_code": "RPharma-2022-rinpharma_290",
  "pdf_url": "https://youtu.be/wPS1J7tjTOs",
  "source_url": "https://rinpharma.github.io/data-pipelines/output/processed_talks.csv",
  "abstract": "Increasingly biostatisticians in pharma companies would like to use R on a daily basis, e.g. the growing number of participants in R/Pharma conferences is one metric showing this trend. As R programs replace proprietary software in this regulated industry, the requirements for quality and reliability increase, e.g. validation of packages might be required. More importantly, programs used in multiple projects or over a longer time period with changing biostatisticians need to be maintainable, intuitive and reliable. Getting this done takes experience and time. In particular, it is challenging to do this as a side project next to other daily biostatistics work and without the right tools in place. Therefore forming a dedicated team, working together closely with the applied biostatisticians, methods experts and IT professionals, can help. We share our Statistical Engineering team experience in Roche, covering agile ways of working, resourcing, product prioritization, and open source collaborations. We believe that taking the Research Software Engineering aspects seriously and adopting an Open Source mindset is key to sustainably and reliably use R in Pharma.",
  "keywords": [],
  "lang": "en",
  "region": "Global",
  "added_at": "2026-08-06T08:04:34+00:00"
 },
 {
