 {
  "id": "R-PHARMA-RPHARMA-2022-RINPHARMA_313",
  "title": "Introducing gtreg: an R package to produce regulatory tables for clinical research",
  "authors": [
   "Shannon Pileggi",
   "Daniel Sjoberg"
  ],
  "year": 2022,
  "conference": "r-pharma",
  "conference_name": "R/Pharma",
  "section_code": "TK",
  "section_name": "Talk",
  "paper_code": "RPharma-2022-rinpharma_313",
  "pdf_url": "https://youtu.be/Vo2v_Krqd_w",
  "source_url": "https://rinpharma.github.io/data-pipelines/output/processed_talks.csv",
  "abstract": "gtreg internally leverages gtsummary to streamline production for regulatory tables in clinical research. There are three functions to assist with adverse event reporting tbl_ae_count(), tbl_ae(), and tbl_ae_focus(); tbl_ae_count() tabulates all AEs observed, whereas both tbl_ae() and tbl_ae_focus() count a single AE per subject by maximum grade. Furthermore, tbl_reg_summary() produces standard data summary tables often used in regulatory submissions and 'tbl_listing()' enables a formatted grouped printing of raw AE listings. All functions are highly customizable to make your regulatory reporting a breeze!",
  "keywords": [],
  "lang": "en",
  "region": "Global",
  "added_at": "2026-08-06T08:04:34+00:00"
 },
 {
  "id": "R-PHARMA-RPHARMA-2022-RINPHARMA_314",
  "title": "RMarkdown for enhanced Quality Control & Documentation",
  "authors": [
   "Patrick Hilden"
  ],
  "year": 2022,
  "conference": "r-pharma",
  "conference_name": "R/Pharma",
  "section_code": "TK",
  "section_name": "Talk",
  "paper_code": "RPharma-2022-rinpharma_314",
  "pdf_url": "https://youtu.be/lPRBoZeI01s",
  "source_url": "https://rinpharma.github.io/data-pipelines/output/processed_talks.csv",
  "abstract": "When working with big data sources, such as medical claims data, the process of data review and quality control (QC) can be both complex and tedious. R and RMarkdown have become common tools for data analytics and report writing in the pharmaceutical space. RMarkdown’s ability to integrate both the code used to query the data, with the results and visualization of it, provides a more powerful interface in which the output can contain both the process and the results, unifying two procedures which are separate with other approaches to the QC process. We present our analytical QC pipeline process which can be developed at the start of a new project and marries the processes of deeply understanding the underlying data in the early stages, with developing an ongoing pipeline of reports and QC procedures which can be automated and run in the future when the data is refreshed. The reduced timeline of this process greatly increases the speed in which updated data can be ingested accurately and confidently, and results in key stakeholders having quick access to the most up to date information in downstream processes and decision making.",
  "keywords": [],
  "lang": "en",
  "region": "Global",
  "added_at": "2026-08-06T08:04:34+00:00"
 },
 {
  "id": "R-PHARMA-RPHARMA-2022-RINPHARMA_315",
  "title": "Data Science in the Pharmaceutical Industry: A Coursera Specialisation",
  "authors": [
   "Kieran Martin"
  ],
  "year": 2022,
  "conference": "r-pharma",
  "conference_name": "R/Pharma",
  "section_code": "TK",
  "section_name": "Talk",
  "paper_code": "RPharma-2022-rinpharma_315",
  "pdf_url": "https://youtu.be/Ocs7TN2Yauc",
  "source_url": "https://rinpharma.github.io/data-pipelines/output/processed_talks.csv",
  "abstract": "The Pharmaceutical industry is adopting new tools and technologies, putting pressure on individuals to learn many new skills in a short period of time. In order to both promote these new ways of working, and to assist those adopting it, at Genentech we are building a new Coursera specialisation. In this talk I will share details of what this specialisation will cover and when you can expect it to be available. I will discuss the different aspects of data science we chose to focus on, and how we are going to promote the use of pharmaverse tools for clinical reporting.",
  "keywords": [],
  "lang": "en",
  "region": "Global",
  "added_at": "2026-08-06T08:04:34+00:00"
 },
 {
  "id": "R-PHARMA-RPHARMA-2022-RINPHARMA_316",
  "title": "Panel Discussion - Finding A Way: Career stories from 4 senior level women in data science",
