 {
  "id": "R-PHARMA-RPHARMA-2024-RINPHARMA_410",
  "title": "Summer is Coming: AI for R, Shiny, and Pharma",
  "authors": [
   "Joe Cheng"
  ],
  "year": 2024,
  "conference": "r-pharma",
  "conference_name": "R/Pharma",
  "section_code": "KN",
  "section_name": "Keynote",
  "paper_code": "RPharma-2024-rinpharma_410",
  "pdf_url": "https://youtu.be/AfMa1CVUdXU",
  "source_url": "https://rinpharma.github.io/data-pipelines/output/processed_talks.csv",
  "abstract": "R users tend to be skeptical of modern AI models, given our weird insistence on answers being accurate, or at least supported by the data. But I believe the time has come—or maybe it’s a little late—for even the most AI-cynical among us to push past their discomfort and get informed about what these tools are truly capable of. And key to that is moving beyond using AI-enabled apps, and towards building our own scripts, packages, and apps that make judicious use of AI. In this talk, I’ll tell you why I believe AI has more to offer the R community than just wrong answers from chat windows or mediocre code suggestions in our IDEs. I’ll also introduce brand-new tools we’re developing at Posit that put powerful AI tools within reach of every R user. And finally, I’ll show how adding some AI could make your next Shiny app dramatically more useful for your users.",
  "keywords": [],
  "lang": "en",
  "region": "Global",
  "added_at": "2026-08-06T08:04:34+00:00"
 },
