 {
  "id": "R-PHARMA-RPHARMA-2024-RINPHARMA_412",
  "title": "From hours to minutes: accelerating your tidymodels code",
  "authors": [
   "Simon Couch"
  ],
  "year": 2024,
  "conference": "r-pharma",
  "conference_name": "R/Pharma",
  "section_code": "TK",
  "section_name": "Talk",
  "paper_code": "RPharma-2024-rinpharma_412",
  "pdf_url": "https://youtu.be/pTMiDHFIiPQ",
  "source_url": "https://rinpharma.github.io/data-pipelines/output/processed_talks.csv",
  "abstract": "This talk demonstrates a 145-fold speedup in training time for a machine learning pipeline with tidymodels through 4 small changes. By adapting a grid search on a canonical model to use a more performant modeling engine, hooking into a parallel computing framework, transitioning to an optimized search strategy, and defining the grid to search over carefully, users can drastically cut down on the time to develop machine learning models with tidymodels without sacrificing predictive performance.",
  "keywords": [],
  "lang": "en",
  "region": "Global",
  "added_at": "2026-08-06T08:04:34+00:00"
 },
 {
  "id": "R-PHARMA-RPHARMA-2024-RINPHARMA_413",
  "title": "From Annoying to Automated: Running Tests with GitHub Actions",
  "authors": [
   "Veerle Eeftink - van Leemput"
  ],
  "year": 2024,
  "conference": "r-pharma",
  "conference_name": "R/Pharma",
  "section_code": "TK",
  "section_name": "Talk",
  "paper_code": "RPharma-2024-rinpharma_413",
  "pdf_url": "https://youtu.be/F8KwNPHiI0U",
  "source_url": "https://rinpharma.github.io/data-pipelines/output/processed_talks.csv",
  "abstract": "Testing is important—we all get that. But let's be honest, writing tests isn't exactly everyone's favorite part of coding. And when you finally do write those tests, there's the added task of making sure they actually cover your code and run every time you make changes. Sounds like a hassle, right? In just 10 minutes, Veerle shows you how to tackle this with ease! From general code coverage to Shiny app testing with shinytest2, she covers how to automate it all using covr and GitHub Actions. Join her for a fun, bite-sized crash course on testing, test coverage, and making testing a little less annoying!",
  "keywords": [],
  "lang": "en",
  "region": "Global",
  "added_at": "2026-08-06T08:04:34+00:00"
 },
 {
  "id": "R-PHARMA-RPHARMA-2024-RINPHARMA_414",
  "title": "The R Validation Hubs Year Ahead",
  "authors": [
   "Doug Kelkhoff"
  ],
  "year": 2024,
  "conference": "r-pharma",
  "conference_name": "R/Pharma",
  "section_code": "TK",
  "section_name": "Talk",
  "paper_code": "RPharma-2024-rinpharma_414",
  "pdf_url": "https://youtu.be/Oe1vQiswccs",
  "source_url": "https://rinpharma.github.io/data-pipelines/output/processed_talks.csv",
  "abstract": "The R Validation Hub is at the precipice of change. This year marks a high water mark the R Validation Hub, culminating in spirited community meetings and adopter feedback. Stemming from more intensive adoption of our tools and guidelines, we want to channel this enthusiasm into a clearer picture for our future. In this short talk we'll cover what we've learned from our adopters and how we plan to incorporate that feedback. Join to hear about upcoming changes to the R Validation Hub's tools ecosystems, governance and new ways to get involved.",
  "keywords": [],
  "lang": "en",
  "region": "Global",
  "added_at": "2026-08-06T08:04:34+00:00"
 },
 {
  "id": "R-PHARMA-RPHARMA-2024-RINPHARMA_415",
  "title": "Accelerating Cancer Drug Discovery: Harnessing the Power of tempusverse on the Tempus Lens Platform",
  "authors": [
   "Nitesh Turaga"
  ],
  "year": 2024,
  "conference": "r-pharma",
  "conference_name": "R/Pharma",
  "section_code": "TK",
  "section_name": "Talk",
  "paper_code": "RPharma-2024-rinpharma_415",
  "pdf_url": "https://youtu.be/DVGj985N0Ow",
  "source_url": "https://rinpharma.github.io/data-pipelines/output/processed_talks.csv",
  "abstract": "The use of real-world evidence (RWE) has become increasingly crucial for drug discovery and development. However, researchers often face challenges in standardizing clinical and molecular approaches to efficiently analyze and interpret vast amounts of data from multiple sources. To transform the analytical process, we developed tempusverse, a suite of R packages to analyze Tempus and public datasets on the Tempus Lens Workspaces platform. The tempusverse is a comprehensive collection of production-ready R packages designed with modularity, reproducibility, and robust versioning in mind. This thoughtful design not only streamlines the analysis of one of the world's largest real-world cancer databases but also ensures research integrity is preserved throughout the analytical process. The packages offer standardized methodology for data wrangling, analysis, and visualization, enabling researchers to gain fast insights and make informed decisions rapidly. By combining the power of tempusverse with the production-grade workspace environment provided by the Tempus Lens platform, researchers can seamlessly integrate public data sources, efficiently process information, and generate publication-ready visualizations. The symbiotic relationship between tempusverse and Lens empowers pharmaceutical researchers to accelerate the discovery of novel cancer therapeutics while maintaining the highest standards of scientific rigor. In this session, we will demonstrate how this innovative approach enhances decision-making, increases the probability of technical success in clinical trials, and ultimately improves patient outcomes. Join us to explore how the tempusverse, coupled with the Lens platform, is revolutionizing the way we leverage real-world evidence in cancer drug discovery, all while ensuring the reproducibility and integrity of research findings.",
  "keywords": [],
  "lang": "en",
  "region": "Global",
  "added_at": "2026-08-06T08:04:34+00:00"
 },
